# --- LLM provider (pick one) -------------------------------------------------
# If several are configured, `_build_llm` picks in this order:
# Azure OpenAI > local server > plain OpenAI.
#
# Option A: Azure OpenAI (used automatically if both vars below are set)
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=
AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-5
AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-12-01-preview

# Option B: OpenAI
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1

# Option C: local, OpenAI-API-compatible server (Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp
# server, vLLM...) — no API key/cost. Pick a model that supports tool calling,
# e.g. `ollama pull qwen2.5:7b-instruct` then set the two lines below.
# Leave LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL unset to run via docker-compose: it already points
# agent-api at host.docker.internal, since `localhost` inside the container
# means the container itself, not your machine.
# LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b-instruct
# LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=not-needed

# --- MCP transport ------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset (default): the agent spawns the scoring server as a local stdio
# subprocess, so `python -m agent.agent SME-000001` needs nothing running.
# Set: the agent connects over HTTP instead, and the scoring server must
# already be up (`make mcp-http`, or the `mcp` service in docker-compose,
# which sets this for you).
# FINRISK_MCP_URL=http://localhost:8000/mcp

# --- Langfuse observability (optional — agent runs without tracing if unset) --
LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=
LANGFUSE_HOST=https://cloud.langfuse.com

# --- ML pipeline overrides (optional, all have sane defaults) -----------------
FINRISK_DECISION_THRESHOLD=0.30
FINRISK_MODEL_VERSION=1.0.0
# lightgbm (default) or logistic_regression — the latter trades a little
# precision at the threshold for a directly interpretable coefficient per
# feature. Re-run train + eval after changing it.
# FINRISK_MODEL_TYPE=lightgbm

# --- MLflow (MLOps) -----------------------------------------------------------
# MLflow is the storage layer, not optional instrumentation: every model,
# preprocessor, held-out split, metric and plot lives in a run, and the MCP
# server serves whichever version wears the `champion` alias. There is no
# local-file fallback, so `make train` must have run before the server starts.
# Browse the store with `make mlflow-ui` (http://localhost:5000).
# FINRISK_MLFLOW_DIR=./mlruns                 # local file store (default)
# FINRISK_MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=http://mlflow.internal:5000   # or a shared server
# FINRISK_MLFLOW_EXPERIMENT=finrisk-credit-risk
# FINRISK_MLFLOW_REGISTERED_MODEL=finrisk-credit-risk
# FINRISK_MLFLOW_MODEL_ALIAS=champion         # which alias the server serves
